Master’s degree in Human Resources Management or other business-related fields is an added advantage;
A professional certificate in the Institute of Chartered Institute of Personnel Management (“CIPM”) or other similar HR certification is required and demonstration of practical knowledge of Nigerian Labour Law.
Essential Skills:
Excellent interpersonal relationship building and employee coaching skills;
Ability to multitask, prioritize, and manage time efficiently;
Must be a goal-oriented, organized team player;
Must be a creative problem solver who thrives when presented with a challenge;
Ability to mentor and lead;
Ability to present company mission and history clearly and confidently;
Excellent Information Communication Technology (“ICT”) skills including Excel, PowerPoint, and Word (must be at least 80% proficient); and
Must possess a great professional attitude.
